Description: CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 for PHP 5.6, on top of backport-php2shell-1.patch: what the official fix and the other 5.6 ports have and that patch has not. $_GET, $_POST, $_COOKIE and their sub-arrays start as the smallest array (2 buckets: nTableMask 0 marks an uninitialized table in PHP 5), as the singleton arrays of the official fix; EG(error_handling) and EG(exception) are reset right after the object store is freed, where the official fix does it, so that an error in the rest of the shutdown cannot reach the freed exception; EG(exception_class) is reset with the handlers; SG(callback_func), the header callback of the request, is reset after it; "Out of memory" of the persistent allocator wrappers ends with _exit() instead of exit(), so that no atexit handler runs in that state.
Origin: azsupport, from our port of 22.10.2026 (131fde85f): the singleton arrays and the early reset from php-src 802c21075308 (PHP 7.4, Arnaud Le Blanc), SG(callback_func) from the 5.6 port of Ondrej Sury (php5.6 5.6.40-104, debian/patches/0261-Avoid-state-corruption-via-bailout.patch)

diff --git a/Zend/zend_API.c b/Zend/zend_API.c
index 0757cc926..946016605 100644
--- a/Zend/zend_API.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_API.c
@@ -1016,6 +1016,18 @@ ZEND_API int _array_init(zval *arg, uint size ZEND_FILE_LINE_DC) /* {{{ */
 }
 /* }}} */
 
+/* The smallest array: $_GET, $_POST, $_COOKIE and their sub-arrays start with
+ * it, so that request variables cost as little memory as possible (the
+ * "singleton" arrays of the official fix). nTableMask == 0 marks a table that is
+ * not initialized yet in PHP 5, so 2 is the smallest size that works. */
+ZEND_API int _array_init_singleton(zval *arg ZEND_FILE_LINE_DC) /* {{{ */
+{
+	_array_init(arg, 0 ZEND_FILE_LINE_RELAY_CC);
+	Z_ARRVAL_P(arg)->nTableSize = 2;
+	return SUCCESS;
+}
+/* }}} */
+
 static int zend_merge_property(zval **value TSRMLS_DC, int num_args, va_list args, const zend_hash_key *hash_key) /* {{{ */
 {
 	/* which name should a numeric property have ? */
